{
  "requirement": "`FileEvidenceStorage::new` retains the root directory without touching the filesystem.\nThe store implements `Send` and `Sync`. Its `load` and `store` futures are `Send`.\n\n`Record`, `Dependency`, and `Fingerprint` support Serde when their type\nparameters do. `Criterion::Ok` is always serializable; its JSON value is\nalready in the record. Serialization bounds on node identities and edge labels\napply when using this helper.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs` cover each obligation of `requirements.sdk.filesystem-storage.interface`.\n\n**`new` retains the root without touching the filesystem.**\n- `fn[paths_are_injective_and_loading_missing_records_has_no_side_effects]` builds the store on a root that does not exist. It asserts `record_path` equals `root.join(expected)` for many node paths, so the root is retained. After all the loads it asserts `!root.exists()`.\n- `fn[send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys]` asserts `!root.exists()` right after `new`, with a deeper missing root.\n\n**`Send` and `Sync` on the store.**\n- `fn[concurrent_readers_only_observe_complete_records_from_competing_writes]` wraps the store in an `Arc` and uses it from several scoped threads. That compiles only if `FileEvidenceStorage` is `Send + Sync`.\n- This is a compile-time check, which suits a type-level obligation.\n\n**`load` and `store` futures are `Send`.**\n- `fn[send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys]` passes both `store.store(...)` and `store.load(...)` through the local helper `send<T: Send>`. The test fails to compile if either future is not `Send`.\n\n**Serde support for `Record`, `Dependency` and `Fingerprint` when their type parameters support it.**\n- `fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]` round-trips a `Record<String, ()>`. It asserts the version, the dependencies (both `Dependency::Node` and `OutgoingEdges`, each with a `Fingerprint`) and the JSON output.\n- The same test round-trips a `Record<String, String>` with a non-unit edge label, `\"tests/é\"`, and asserts the dependencies are equal.\n- It also loads with `u8` for the node and edge parameters and asserts `FileStorageError::Json`. This shows the serialization bounds on node identities and edge labels apply.\n- `fn[consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path]` adds a round trip through the consumer delegation path.\n\n**`Criterion::Ok` is always serializable and its JSON value is already in the record.**\n- The helper stores and loads the record's `output`, a `serde_json::Value`, and the tests assert it is unchanged.\n- `Criterion::Ok` is declared with `Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send` bounds, so no extra case needs testing.\n\nI found no gaps and no missing {test} markings. The tests carry the `interface` {test} reference. No {fixme} acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "4fa7c0209cc8a47ded44aa43c8f5142920833c5dae546977ebf2d7b4b9910690",
